{
 "source": "projects/openet/assets/ensemble/conus/gridmet/monthly/v2_0",
 "unit": "mm",
 "period": [
  1999,
  2024
 ],
 "method": "Field mean of the OpenET ensemble at 30 m; a month counts when at least 90% of the field's pixels have a value. et_min / et_max are the range across the ensemble models. Precipitation and reference ET are gridMET, from the weather CSV. Crop is the CDL majority class.",
 "caveats": [
  "On all five fields, including plain wheat-fallow, mean annual OpenET is about 20% above gridMET precipitation (ET / P 1.19-1.21). A dryland field cannot evaporate more than it receives over 24 years, so OpenET is biased high here relative to gridMET precipitation (or precipitation is biased low). Use OpenET for differences between years, crops and fields, not for the absolute level.",
  "Because the ratio is the same on every field, ET / P does not separate irrigated from dryland fields here.",
  "OpenET models use gridMET reference ET, so OpenET is not fully independent of the weather files."
 ],
